cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or model, please cite it as below, and cite the dataset it was trained on."
type: software
title: "Poultry disease image classification: a ResNet50 prototype with in-browser CAM and an honest external evaluation"
abstract: >-
  A ResNet50 classifier for photos of poultry droppings (Coccidiosis, Healthy, Salmonella, Newcastle disease),
  trained on version 2 of the Machuve et al. dataset and evaluated on the separately collected, PCR-annotated
  version 3. It reaches 96.7% accuracy on the internal test set and 79.5% on the PCR-confirmed set. Includes a
  Python package and a TensorFlow.js web app with class activation maps that runs entirely in the browser.
  Research and decision-support prototype; not a veterinary diagnosis.
